{"id":"99c84636-22c8-4fe1-b4c8-31d848c6ac1c","object":"chat.completion","created":1785029394,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate case structure\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dict\\\")\\n    if 'text' not in case or not isinstance(case['text'], str):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must have a 'text' string\\\")\\n    if 'passes' not in case or not isinstance(case['passes'], list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must have a 'passes' list\\\")\\n    passes = case['passes']\\n    if len(passes) == 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"passes list must not be empty\\\")\\n    for i, p in enumerate(passes):\\n        if not isinstance(p, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"pass[{i}] must be a dict\\\")\\n        if 'name' not in p or not isinstance(p['name'], str):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"pass[{i}] missing 'name' (string)\\\")\\n        if 'old' not in p or not isinstance(p['old'], str):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"pass[{i}] missing 'old' (string)\\\")\\n        if 'new' not in p or not isinstance(p['new'], str):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"pass[{i}] missing 'new' (string)\\\")\\n    if 'max_rounds' not in case or not isinstance(case['max_rounds'], int) or case['max_rounds'] < 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must have 'max_rounds' positive integer\\\")\\n    max_rounds = case['max_rounds']\\n\\n    text = case['text']\\n    applications = []\\n    round_num = 0\\n\\n    while True:\\n        changed_in_sweep = False\\n        for p in passes:\\n            old = p['old']\\n            new = p['new']\\n            # Find first occurrence\\n            idx = text.find(old)\\n            if idx != -1:\\n                # Replace only first occurrence\\n                text = text[:idx] + new + text[idx+len(old):]\\n                applications.append(p['name'])\\n                changed_in_sweep = True\\n        if not changed_in_sweep:\\n            # Fixed point reached\\n            fixed_point = True\\n            break\\n        round_num += 1\\n        if round_num >= max_rounds:\\n            fixed_point = False\\n            break\\n\\n    return {\\n        'applications': applications,\\n        'fixed_point': fixed_point,\\n        'text': text\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write Python function solve(case) as per the description. The task is to run a pass schedule to fixed point. The case payload has: text (initial artifact), passes (list of pass objects with name, old, new), max_rounds (integer). Each pass replaces all occurrences of old with new? \"Each pass performs at most its first eligible rewrite per sweep.\" Likely meaning each pass can apply at most one replacement per sweep? Or \"first eligible rewrite\" means the first occurrence? The description: \"Each pass performs at most its first eligible rewrite per sweep.\" That suggests for each pass, in a sweep, it scans the string and replaces the first occurrence of 'old' with 'new' (if present). Then we record passes that change the artifact. Repeat full sweeps until no change or max_rounds reached. Return: applications (list of pass names that changed the artifact in order of application across sweeps? Or list of passes applied? The output schema: applications is array of strings, fixed_point boolean, text final string. From the schema: \"applications\": array of strings. Likely the ordered list of pass names that were applied (i.e., that changed the text) during the entire process. Fixed_point indicates whether we reached fixed point (i.e., last sweep had no changes) or if we stopped due to max_rounds? Should be true if we stopped because no changes (i.e., fixed point reached), false if we stopped due to max_rounds without reaching fixed point? The problem says \"Repeat full sweeps until none changes or the round budget is consumed.\" So fixed_point flag is true if we stopped because no changes (i.e., last sweep no application), false if we stopped because round budget consumed (and still had changes? Actually if round budget consumed, we might stop mid-sweep? But it says \"or the round budget is consumed.\" Likely we stop after completing a sweep that consumed a round, and if we exceed max_rounds? Let's interpret: max_rounds is budget for sweeps. We repeat sweeps; each sweep applies passes in order. If after a sweep, no changes, we're done (fixed_point true). If after a sweep, there were changes, and we have not yet used up max_rounds sweeps, we continue. If we do a sweep and it changes something, and we have used up max_rounds (i.e., round count >= max_rounds), we stop and return current state with fixed_point false. So we track round number (starting at 1). For each sweep, we apply passes in order. For each pass, we look for first occurrence of old in current text. If found, replace it with new (only first occurrence? \"at most its first eligible rewrite per sweep\" suggests we replace only the first occurrence, not all). Then if the text changed, we add pass name to applications list. After processing all passes in a sweep, if any pass changed text, we increment round count; if round count reaches max_rounds and there were changes, we stop with fixed_point false. If no changes in a sweep, fixed_point true. Also if we finish a sweep with changes but round count haven't reached max_rounds, we continue next sweep.\n\nImportant: each pass only replaces first occurrence of old in the current text. That's the \"first eligible rewrite\". Also note that old/new are strings. The pass name is a string. We need to validate fields? The description says validate every required field before computing a result. Raise ValueError for infeasible or structurally invalid case. So we should check that case has text (string), passes (list of dicts with name, old, new as strings), max_rounds (int >0 maybe). Also ensure passes have unique names? Not required but not harmful. Just do basic validation.\n\nImplementation: define solve(case) that returns dict with keys applications, fixed_point, text.\n\nEdge cases: if text empty? Fine. If no pass replaces anything, then applications empty, fixed_point true, text same. If max_rounds is 0? Should raise or treat? Probably max_rounds at least 1. We'll raise if not positive integer.\n\nWe'll implement using while loop with round counter.\n\nNote: \"Perform at most its first eligible rewrite per sweep.\" Means per sweep, each pass can replace at most one occurrence (the first). So we need to find index of old and replace that occurrence. Use str.find, str.replace with count=1.\n\nAlso note: \"Record only passes that change the artifact.\" So we only add to applications if the pass actually changed the text.\n\nWe must not mutate input case. So we copy text initially.\n\nReturn value: Python dict with keys \"applications\", \"fixed_point\", \"text\". Ensure applications is list of strings.\n\nNow produce final answer: JSON with key \"implementation\" containing Python source escaped.\n\nLet's write code.\n\nPossible validation: Check that case is dict, text is string, passes is list, each pass has required keys, max_rounds int >0. If any invalid, raise ValueError.\n\nWe'll write solve function. Use standard library only.\n\nNow produce final JSON."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1314,"completion_tokens":1674,"total_tokens":2988,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1280},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1084},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1280,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":34},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}